  家庭背景 | family background

idioms[4]{hanzi,pinyin,meaning_en}:
  烘云托月 | hōng yún tuō yuè | paint clouds to set off the moon; provide effective background contrast
  源远流长 | yuán yuǎn liú cháng | dating back to a distant past and enduring across time
  错综复杂 | cuò zōng fù zá | intricate, complex, and tangled in context
  追本溯源 | zhuī běn sù yuán | trace back to the primordial source or root context

character_decomposition[2]{character,pinyin,meaning_en,meaning_es,radical,radical_meaning_en,meaning_component,sound_component,stroke_count,composition_type,etymology_and_mnemonic,visual_mnemonic_story_en,visual_mnemonic_story_es,tone_mnemonic_anchor,cangjie,traditional}:
  背 | bèi | back of body; behind; turn away; memorize | espalda; detrás; dar la espalda; memorizar | 月 | flesh | 北 (two persons standing back to back) + 月/肉 (flesh / dorsal human body) | 北 (běi, north / phonetic nuance bèi) | 9 | 上下结构 | Two people standing back to back 北 over flesh 月; represents the dorsal back of the human torso or rear side of objects. | Two figures turning back to back (北) reveal the dorsal spine of the human body (月) as the back (背). | Dos figuras dándose la espalda (北) revelan la espina dorsal del cuerpo (月) marcando la espalda (背). | 51 | LPB | ""
  景 | jǐng | scenery; view; landscape; situation | paisaje; vista; decorado; situación; panorama | 日 | sun | 日 (sun / daylight illumination) + 京 (tall imperial city watchtower) | 京 (jīng, capital / phonetic jǐng) | 12 | 上下结构 | Sunlight 日 illuminating a high imperial pavilion tower 京; radiant scenery, vista, spectacle, and backdrop setting. | Bright sunshine (日) illuminating a towering capital pavilion (京) creates a scenic panorama (景). | La luz del sol (日) iluminando una torre monumental (京) compone un panorama escénico (景). | 214 | AYRF | ""

mnemonics_and_roots:
  composite_memory_hook_en: The scenic panorama (景) resting quietly at the rear back (背) of the main subject constitutes the background (背景).
  composite_memory_hook_es: El decorado escénico (景) que descansa detrás en la parte trasera (背) conforma el fondo o contexto (背景).
  cultural_and_cognitive_roots: Derived from classical theatrical staging: scenery panels hung behind (背) the acting stage to evoke historical place and mood (景).
  tone_sandhi_and_pitch_modulation: Fourth tone followed by third tone: 'bèi jǐng' (51-214). Sharp initial fall dropping into a full low-dip third tone.

traps_and_cognates:
  look_alikes[4]{character,pinyin,meaning_en,distinction_note}:
    肯 | kěn | willing; agree | Has 止 at top over 月 instead of 北 in 背
    胄 | zhòu | helmet; descendant | Has 由 over 月
    影 | yǐng | shadow; film | Has hair/pattern radical 彡 on right of 景
    晾 | liàng | air-dry in sun | Has 日 on left of 京 instead of on top in 景
  etymological_cognates[4]{character,pinyin,gloss_en}:
